# IRIS — Intelligent Release & Image Staging
# Keep credentials, device images, and generated artifacts OUT of the repo.
# NOTE: *.example files are intentionally tracked (they are templates, not real config).

# --- credentials / secrets (NEVER commit) ---
creds/*
# the template IS tracked (real creds/deploy.env is not — matched by creds/* above)
!creds/deploy.env.example
.env
*.env
# kubernetes/iris-seed-server.env is a TRACKED template (sentinel values only,
# no secrets): kustomize's configMapGenerator builds the ConfigMap from it.
!kubernetes/iris-seed-server.env
# The console counterpart also contains non-secret defaults only and must be
# tracked or a fresh checkout cannot render the kustomize base.
!kubernetes/iris-console.env
server/.env
tokens.txt
rpc-secret
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
id_rsa*
# the pinned Cisco Bulk Hash verify cert is public material (no private
# key) and must be tracked -- see server/certs/cisco_bulkhash_verify.pem
# for its provenance/fingerprint documentation. Narrowly scoped to this one
# file, not every *.pem under server/certs/, so a future private key or
# other cert dropped in that directory stays ignored by default.
!server/certs/cisco_bulkhash_verify.pem

# --- device images / large firmware binaries ---
*.bin
*.pkg
*.SPA.bin
# Everything an operator stages under images/ is a large, Cisco-proprietary
# artifact, whatever its extension (.bin, .iso, .tar, .rpm today). Ignore the
# whole directory rather than chasing the format list, and re-include only its
# README. `images/*` (not `images/`) is what makes the negation possible: git
# cannot re-include a file inside an ignored DIRECTORY.
images/*
!images/README.md

# --- torrents / aria2 download state ---
*.torrent
*.aria2

# --- handed-in aria2c deliverables (produced by the aria2-next-static
#     project, verified against tools/aria2c.sha256) ---
# The two TESTED clients are committed, so a fresh clone is complete and needs
# no download; tools/get-aria2c.sh verifies them against tools/aria2c.sha256
# and only fetches when one is missing. Everything else that lands here (spare
# `.old-*` builds, experiments, other architectures) stays ignored.
# `deliverables/*` rather than `deliverables/` is what makes the re-inclusion
# possible: git cannot re-include a file inside an ignored DIRECTORY.
deliverables/*
!deliverables/aria2c-x86_64
!deliverables/aria2c-aarch64
agentinfo/

# --- vendored binaries ---
# bin/aria2c is the tested x86_64 client (the same bytes as
# deliverables/aria2c-x86_64) and IS committed and verified against
# tools/aria2c.sha256; tools/get-aria2c.sh reinstalls it only if it is
# missing. Every other binary dropped in bin/ stays ignored.
bin/*
!bin/.gitkeep
!bin/aria2c
tools/bin/

# --- generated release artifacts (rebuilt by tools/make-release.sh) ---
release/
*.tgz
iris-agent.tgz

# --- generated per-device installers + secret-bearing fleet files ---
# (the *.example templates above these are kept)
fleet/dist/
fleet/iris-fleet.conf
fleet/devices.csv
fleet/assignments.csv
fleet/roles.csv

# --- runtime output ---
artifacts/*
!artifacts/.gitkeep

# --- python / test / OS junk ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# --- local opencode / AI-agent tooling (not part of the IRIS deliverable) ---
.opencode/
AGENTS.md

# --- generated documentation output ---
# Public source docs live in docs/ and are intentionally tracked.
site/
deploy/

# --- local status / handoff notes (contain lab IPs + credentials) ---
HANDOFF.md
lab/evidence/

# --- IOx / IOS-XR app build output (generated iris.tar / iris-xr.rpm) ---
device/iox/out/
device/xr/out/
*.rpm
HANDOFF-*.md

# --- host-specific Compose override (lab ports/mounts; never shared) ---
server/docker-compose.override.yml

# --- superpowers brainstorm/visual-companion scratch (local only) ---
.superpowers/

# --- Cisco-licensed typeface: staged at deploy time, never distributed ---
server/webroot/fonts/SharpSans-Bold.woff2

# --- locally built Console React assets (Docker builds these separately) ---
server/webroot/assets/console.js
server/webroot/assets/console.css
